issue.description:
Polish the App shells preview presentation so the examples feel cleaner, more consistent with the system's semantic tokens, and less like elevated cards.

## Goal

Refine the outer presentation of the three App shell examples without redesigning their internal UI.

This ticket covers:

* align Inset project's connected outer shell/sidebar surface with the dedicated Sidebar background token;
* remove outer shell shadows from all App shell examples;
* replace those outer shadows with a restrained semantic ring/border-style edge;
* increase vertical spacing between App shell examples;
* add more separation between the App shells tab row and the first shell example;
* increase App shell labels by one typography step.

The key boundary is that this ticket targets the **outer shell preview framing**, not shadows or elevation used by components inside each shell.

## 1. Inset project: use Sidebar background token

The Inset project currently uses a muted outer shell/sidebar treatment.

Change the connected sidebar / outer shell surface to use the accepted semantic Sidebar background token so it aligns with the other App shell examples.

Requirements:

* use the dedicated `sidebar` background semantic;
* preserve related Sidebar foreground/accent/border behavior where already wired;
* preserve light/dark and theme responsiveness;
* preserve the distinct inset main content panel;
* do not hard-code a one-off color;
* prefer reusing the same Sidebar token treatment/pattern already used by the other App shell previews.

Conceptually:

current:
`bg-muted`

target:
`bg-sidebar`

or the exact accepted equivalent in the current composition.

## 2. Remove outer App shell shadows

Remove the shadow/elevation applied to the **outer shell container itself** for all App shell examples.

This applies to:

* Classic workspace;
* Inset project;
* Compact utility.

Important:

Do **not** remove shadows used by components inside those shells.

Examples of internal treatments that should remain untouched unless source inspection proves they are actually part of the outer framing:

* cards;
* menus/popovers;
* controls;
* inset content surfaces;
* internal panels;
* other component-level elevation.

The target is only the shadow that makes the entire shell preview look like a floating card.

## 3. Replace outer shadow with restrained ring/border edge

After removing the outer shell shadow, preserve visual separation using a subtle semantic ring/border-style edge.

Requirements:

* inspect existing Workbench preview/container patterns first;
* reuse the closest accepted semantic treatment rather than inventing a new one;
* do not hard-code an arbitrary raw color;
* use existing border/ring semantics appropriate for structural framing;
* keep the edge restrained and theme-responsive;
* preserve shell radius and current geometry.

The three App shell previews should use the same outer framing treatment unless source inspection identifies an intentional accepted exception.

## 4. Increase spacing between App shell examples

Increase vertical spacing between the individual App shell preview blocks.

Requirements:

* provide visibly clearer separation between:
  * Classic workspace;
  * Inset project;
  * Compact utility;
* preserve the vertical stacked sequence;
* keep spacing consistent across all three;
* avoid excessive whitespace;
* tune through browser evidence rather than adding arbitrary large gaps.

## 5. Increase spacing below App shells tab row

Add slightly more vertical separation between the App shells tab/navigation row and the first App shell example.

Requirements:

* preserve current tab control size and placement;
* do not redesign the tabs;
* increase only the spacing below the tabs / above the first shell section enough to improve hierarchy;
* keep narrow-width layouts contained.

## 6. Increase App shell labels one typography step

Increase the labels for each shell example by one typography step.

Examples:

* Classic workspace
* Inset project
* Compact utility

Requirements:

* preserve wording;
* preserve foreground semantic color;
* preserve current label placement;
* increase only one typography step from the current implementation;
* do not make labels visually compete with main page/section headings;
* avoid hard-coding a raw pixel size if an accepted typography utility/class already exists.

## 7. Preserve shell internals

Do not change:

* shell identities;
* sidebar nav content;
* workspace switchers;
* active nav behavior;
* collapse behavior;
* preview-local collapse isolation;
* Workbench sidebar isolation;
* internal main-panel compositions;
* Theme v3;
* UI Effects;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry;
* dependencies;
* network behavior.

No internal shell redesign is part of this ticket.

## 8. Accessibility and responsiveness

Preserve:

* keyboard/focus behavior;
* sidebar collapse controls;
* icon-only accessibility;
* logical reading order;
* responsive containment;
* no page-level horizontal overflow;
* light/dark contrast.

Spacing and framing changes must not regress shell containment or collapse behavior.

## 9. Verification

Verify at minimum:

* Inset project's connected outer shell/sidebar surface uses the semantic Sidebar background treatment;
* Classic workspace, Inset project, and Compact utility outer shell containers no longer use their previous outer shadow;
* internal component shadows remain unchanged;
* all three shells use the accepted restrained semantic ring/border framing;
* spacing between shell examples is increased consistently;
* spacing between App shells tabs and first shell example is increased appropriately;
* shell labels are one typography step larger;
* shell label wording/color/placement remain unchanged;
* light/dark mode remains coherent;
* built-in/custom themes remain coherent;
* collapse/isolation behavior remains intact;
* narrow/wide layouts remain contained.

## Acceptance

* Inset project outer/sidebar surface uses the dedicated Sidebar background semantic rather than muted.
* Outer shell shadows are removed from all App shell previews.
* Internal component shadows are preserved.
* A restrained semantic ring/border-style edge replaces the outer shell shadow.
* Vertical spacing between App shell examples is increased.
* Spacing between the App shells tab row and first shell example is increased.
* App shell labels are one typography step larger using the existing typography system.
* Existing shell behavior, Theme v3, UI Effects, persistence, Design Command, mutation, registry, dependency, and network boundaries remain unchanged.
